Description: hackable, minimal, fast TUI file explorer
 xplr browses the filesystem from a terminal interface, and is built to be
 wired into other tools: every action can be scripted in Lua, and it prints
 its result to standard output so a shell function can act on the selection.
 .
 It ships no file operations of its own beyond navigation and selection.
 Copying, moving and deleting are done by the messages a configuration sends,
 which is what makes it small and what makes it worth configuring.
